From: conda-forge go-feedstock maintainers <noreply@conda-forge.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/cgo/internal/test: support Windows Clang complex types

MSVC's complex.h does not provide the C99 complex macro consistently,
and UCRT headers can instead define it as the legacy _complex struct.
Clang supports the underlying _Complex keyword when targeting the MSVC
ABI, so normalize the macro locally to keep issue 8694's complex-macro
coverage on native Windows ARM64.
---
 src/cmd/cgo/internal/test/issue8694.go | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cmd/cgo/internal/test/issue8694.go b/src/cmd/cgo/internal/test/issue8694.go
--- a/src/cmd/cgo/internal/test/issue8694.go
+++ b/src/cmd/cgo/internal/test/issue8694.go
@@ -9,6 +9,13 @@ package cgotest
 /*
 #include <complex.h>
 
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && defined(__clang__)
+#ifdef complex
+#undef complex
+#endif
+#define complex _Complex
+#endif
+
 complex float complexFloatSquared(complex float a) { return a*a; }
 complex double complexDoubleSquared(complex double a) { return a*a; }
 */
-- 
